        <h3 style="margin-bottom:1rem;font-size:1.3rem;">Understanding Water Contamination</h3>
        <p style="color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:1.25rem;line-height:1.8;">Water pollution occurs when harmful substances contaminate a water body, degrading quality and rendering it toxic to humans or the environment. Our platform provides a comprehensive tool for analysis.</p>
        <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.75rem;">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.75rem;"><span style="color:var(--green);font-size:1.1rem;">✔</span><span style="color:var(--muted);font-size:0.9rem;">Chemical pollution from factories and agriculture</span></div>
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.75rem;"><span style="color:var(--green);font-size:1.1rem;">✔</span><span style="color:var(--muted);font-size:0.9rem;">Microbiological contamination from untreated sewage</span></div>
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.75rem;"><span style="color:var(--green);font-size:1.1rem;">✔</span><span style="color:var(--muted);font-size:0.9rem;">Nutrient pollution causing harmful algal blooms</span></div>
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.75rem;"><span style="color:var(--green);font-size:1.1rem;">✔</span><span style="color:var(--muted);font-size:0.9rem;">Radiological and noise pollution in water bodies</span></div>
